description:
This question resolves **YES** if, between 1 January 2026 and 31 December 2026 (UTC), any of the following entities publishes a Sudan-war total **excess-mortality estimate (direct + indirect)** with a **central / point estimate exceeding 200,000 deaths**, applied at **nationwide** scope (i.e., covering "Sudan", "the Sudan war", or "the conflict" - not a single state, single city, or single event):

1. A peer-reviewed article in a PubMed-indexed medical or epidemiological journal (the *Lancet* family, *BMJ* family, *NEJM*, *JAMA*, *PLOS*, *Nature*, *Science*, *Conflict and Health*, or similar);
2. A working paper or preprint by a named academic research group with a university affiliation, hosted on SSRN, medRxiv, ResearchGate, or an institutional site (e.g., LSHTM Sudan Research Group, Yale Humanitarian Research Lab, UCLouvain CRED);
3. A formal publication of a UN body (UN Independent International Fact-Finding Mission for Sudan, OHCHR, OCHA, WHO, UNICEF) presenting the figure as the body's own estimate, not a citation of others;
4. A formal report or press release with stated methodology from a major international NGO with epidemiological capacity (MSF, ICRC, IRC, Save the Children, or similar);
5. A national government report (US State Department, UK FCDO, EU EUAA, or similar) presenting its own modelled figure (not a citation);
6. A documented release or revision of the [CRED EM-DAT](https://www.emdat.be/) or [Uppsala UCDP](https://ucdp.uu.se/) database that lists a Sudan-war cumulative total exceeding the threshold, accompanied by a public report or release note.

This question resolves **NO** if no such publication appears by 31 December 2026 (UTC).
